Read CLAUDE.md.

Implement Sprint 3.1: the agent runtime. Temporal outer workflow,
LangGraph inner cognitive graph, typed tool bus.

Deliverables:

1. Temporal: deploy a single-node Temporal server in Compose (or use
   Temporal Cloud — document the choice in CLAUDE.md addendum). Create
   namespaces: `ratify` (default) and `ratify-test`. Task queues:
   `agent-default`, `agent-batch`.

2. agents/ Python package:
   - Temporal worker (`agents/worker.py`) connects to `agent-default`.
   - LangGraph graph definitions in `agents/graphs/` — one per agent type.
   - Every graph node executes as a Temporal Activity. No node calls a
     tool directly outside an Activity. Durability comes from Temporal;
     do not add a LangGraph checkpointer.
   - Tool bus client in `agents/tools.py`: each tool is an HTTP call to
     the Go API with a service JWT. Tools: score_lead, get_deal_context,
     get_account_context, draft_email, get_recent_activities.

3. Tool registration: `internal/toolbus/registry.go` in the Go side.
   Each tool declares: name, input schema (JSON), required permission
   (e.g., `lead:read`, `deal:read`), read vs write. Write tools are
   refused if called without a decision-gate token — Sprint 3.2 will
   issue those tokens; for now, write tools are disabled entirely.

4. Agent service accounts: `agent_worker` database role, SELECT only on
   the tables each tool needs. The agent runtime connects as
   `agent_worker`, never `app_user`.

5. Agent run orchestration:
   - POST /api/v1/agents/{agent_name}/runs starts a Temporal workflow.
   - Returns a run_id. Client polls GET /api/v1/agents/runs/{id}.
   - Status: pending, running, completed, failed. On failure, include
     the trace.

6. Tests:
   - A multi-step tool loop (score_lead → get_account_context →
     complete) survives a worker crash mid-run and completes on restart.
   - No duplicate tool invocations after crash.
   - A write tool (draft_email saved to sequence) is refused when called
     without a decision-gate token — even in a test.
   - Tool calls respect permissions: agent_worker cannot SELECT from a
     table it lacks grants for.

Acceptance criteria:
- `make test` green.
- A read-only agent run completes end-to-end within 30 seconds.
- Worker crash test passes.
- No agent can write to CRM tables.

Commit when green.